# RAL CPU array: the hpc_ral_cpu interferometer cells of jvla.
# Likelihood-lifecycle phase 2b interferometer campaign (autolens_profiling#469), batch 1: 8 leg(s).
# GENERATED by scripts/misc/campaigns/interferometer_p2b.py --write; edit the generator,
# not this file (the campaign test fails on a hand edit). The batch procedure is in
# scripts/misc/campaigns/README.md.
#
# LIBRARY CODE. A private checkout of the five libraries at tag 2026.10.25.1 ($PYAUTO_PRIVATE_BASE,
# default /mnt/ral/jnightin/profiling/PyAuto_2026.10.25.1) is prepended to PYTHONPATH over the shared venv
# ($PYAUTO_HPC_BASE, default /mnt/ral/jnightin/PyAuto, third-party packages only; finufft 2.5.1
# serves the NumPy NUFFT). The job refuses to run if a library imports from anywhere
# else or sits at another tag, and after each leg it checks the row's library_revisions
# equal the checkout's HEADs. The shared mirror is never pulled or used. AP_ROOT is the
# checkout this was submitted from (hpc/<batch>/../..).
#
# CELLS. Every pixelized leg runs the standard-size interferometer production cell
# (--standard-size, ruling R3: Delaunay 1250 Hilbert + 30 zeroed edge points with
# AdaptSplit, rectangular 35x35 RectangularBilinearAdaptImage with Adapt, the truth
# lensed-source adapt image uncapped; MGE-20 unchanged) and writes its row, fit.png and
# parity.json into the mirrored cell named by --output-path under the gitignored
# output/p2b_batch1/ scratch tree, never in place over committed rows.
#
# MEMORY. --mem=64gb from batch 0's sacct MaxRSS (bounding instrument) x 1.5,
# at least 32 GB.
# One leg per array task on `ral` (CPU work never goes on `gpu`). numba legs pin their
# BLAS and numba threads to 1; JAX CPU legs get NPROC=8.
#
# WALL-BASIS: measured by batch 0. Each leg's wall is that of its batch-0 leg of the
# same script, setup and host class on the bounding instrument, the larger of the
# walls.tsv WALL and sacct Elapsed; --time is 1.25x the total plus
# 15 min of slack, rounded up to the next 30 min.
#   2 leg(s): delaunay jax_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde breakdown, delaunay jax_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde runtime
#   cell: interferometer/delaunay/jvla  device: ral_cpu  precision: fp64
#   source: measured-wall  wall: 1215  ref: 413115_0,413115_1  measured-on: jvla  headroom: 1.25  median: included
#   2 leg(s): delaunay numba_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde breakdown, delaunay numba_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde runtime
#   cell: interferometer/delaunay_numba/jvla  device: ral_cpu  precision: fp64
#   source: measured-wall  wall: 5541  ref: 413115_2,413115_3  measured-on: jvla  headroom: 1.25  median: included
#   2 leg(s): rectangular jax_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde breakdown, rectangular jax_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde runtime
#   cell: interferometer/pixelization/jvla  device: ral_cpu  precision: fp64
#   source: measured-wall  wall: 943  ref: 413115_8,413115_9  measured-on: jvla  headroom: 1.25  median: included
#   2 leg(s): rectangular numba_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde breakdown, rectangular numba_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde runtime
#   cell: interferometer/pixelization_numba/jvla  device: ral_cpu  precision: fp64
#   source: measured-wall  wall: 6461  ref: 413115_10,413115_11  measured-on: jvla  headroom: 1.25  median: included

#SBATCH -J p2b_interferometer_ral_cpu_jvla
